e's a summary of the session notes in 8 bullet points:\n\n- **Scope & context:** A two-part rebuild series of the `llama.cpp-sycl-f16-git` AUR package (Raudbjorn fork) on host `vinbonesjr` (Ryzen 7900X3D, Intel Arc A770 16GB), spanning 2026-09-26 to 2026-10-01, covering commits b10146\u2192b12321 across Context A (Claude Opus 5.5) and Context B (Claude Sonnet 5.5, resumed).\n\n- **Major technical work:** The session addressed a PKGBUILD rework, an LLAMA_SUBPROCESS ABI compatibility trap, SYCL graph optimizations, a oneAPI 2026.0\u21922026.1 upgrade (with DLE swap), oneDNN A/B testing, a DG2 XMX-gather IGC crash patch, 256-GRF kernels, and a 12-vs-18 tokens/second decode investigation.\n\n- **Driver transition:** The Intel Arc A770 switched from the i915 driver (kernel 7.3.0-rc1) to the **xe** driver (kernel 7.3.0-rc5) between the two contexts, accomplished by other sessions.\n\n- **Final state:** The session concluded with a working build, updated systemd service, and a documented footprint; benchmark data and tables were saved to `~/research-llama.cpp/sycl-oneapi-benchmarks-2026-09-27/` and `\u2026-2026-10-01/`, with evidence files in `~"}